<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cao Huan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">246–302</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Also known as Emperor Yuan of Wei</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cao Huan was the last emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cao-wei">Cao Wei</a>, reigning from 260 to 266 as a figurehead under the Sima family. During his reign Wei conquered Shu Han in 263. In 266 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-jin">Sima Yan</a> forced him to abdicate and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-jin-dynasty">Western Jin dynasty</a>, granting Cao Huan the title Prince of Chenliu, which he held until his death.</p></div>
